  "description": "<p>Arizona State University is a public research university in the Phoenix metropolitan area. It is one of the largest public universities by enrollment in the United States.</p><p>Founded in 1885, the University offers a rich history of academic prowess to students worldwide. More than 158 countries are represented in the student body, as over 13,000 international students enroll every year. This makes ASU the number one university for international students.</p><h2>What is the Arizona State University acceptance rate for International Students?</h2><p>The Arizona State University acceptance rate is 88%.</p> <P> Numerous computer labs, online learning resources, and multimedia classrooms combine to create an empowered student experience. Student well-being is protected by counselling, healthcare, and career advice. Fitness centers, swimming pools, and sports fields are all state-of-the-art facilities that allow students to indulge in recreational activities.</p> <p><strong>Student Life</strong></p> <p>Students are part of a community at Arizona State University that values integration and empowered voices. Over 1000 student clubs are run by peers that range from sororities to cultural clubs. The Educational Outreach and Student Services encourages students to make their voices heard. Numerous intramural sports leagues are available for students who are sporty by nature.</p>",
