    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>Arizona State University is a public research university in the Phoenix metropolitan area. It is one of the largest public universities by enrollment in the United States.</p><p>Founded in 1885, the University offers a rich history of academic prowess to students worldwide. More than 158 countries are represented in the student body, as over 13,000 international students enroll every year. This makes ASU the number one university for international students.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>International students are welcome to stay on campus during their time at ASU. Most first-year students enjoy the experience of residing in traditional residence halls consisting of double-occupancy rooms with community bathrooms and communal areas. Suite-style living is another option if students want more privacy but are happy to share a living room and bathroom with fewer people. Students can live independently via apartment-style living, with individual bedrooms and shared common areas providing a nice balance.</p><p>The University has partnerships with multiple off-campus housing providers for students to benefit from, and the ASU Housing office can offer advice to students if needed.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Sports",
      "value": "<p>Fitness centers, swimming pools, and sports fields are all state-of-the-art facilities that allow students to indulge in recreational activities.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Lab",
      "value": "<p>Numerous computer labs, online learning resources, and multimedia classrooms combine to create an empowered student experience.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Library",
      "value": "<p>ASU boasts multiple libraries, such as the Hayden Library: the most extensive library on the Tempe campus. It has over four million items and resources. The University is also renowned for offering first-rate research facilities in biotechnology, healthcare, and environmental science.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
